 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account passkeys
+
+Open `/devtools-times/account/passkeys` (also linked from **My account**).
+Password sign-in now establishes an Astro server session. Signed-in users can
+register, list, rename, and remove passkeys; the sign-in page also accepts them.
+Registration and authentication use server-verified WebAuthn challenges that
+expire after five minutes and require user verification.
+
+Use Node.js 24 or newer. Credentials are stored in SQLite under `.data/`;
+set `ACCOUNT_DATA_DIR` to change this directory. Persist this directory and the
+Astro session storage across restarts. Multi-instance deployments require shared
+account and session storage instead of each instance's local filesystem.
+Passkeys require HTTPS in deployment; localhost works for development.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for API authorization, ownership, validation, and challenge tests.
